+http://localhost:8000/docs
+```
+
+### 2. Start the Frontend
+
+Open another terminal, then run:
+
+```bash
+cd frontend
+python -m http.server 8080
+```
+
+Open this in your browser:
+
+```text
+http://localhost:8080
+```
+
+This matches the allowed frontend origins configured in `.env`.
+
+## Environment Variables
+
+The project includes a development `.env` file and `.env.example` template.
+
+```env
+SECRET_KEY=replace-this-with-a-long-random-secret-key-for-production
+ALGORITHM=HS256
+ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=30
+FRONTEND_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080,http://127.0.0.1:8080
+```
+
+For real deployment, replace `SECRET_KEY` with a long random secret and do not commit production secrets.
+
+## Test Credentials
+
+A demo user is seeded when the backend starts:
+
+```text
+Email: user@example.com
+Password: password123
+```
+
+The password is stored as a bcrypt hash, not plain text.
+
+## Manual API Testing
+
+### Register
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/register \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"username":"newuser@example.com","password":"securepass123"}'
+```
+
+### Login
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/token \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
+  -d "username=newuser@example.com&password=securepass123"
+```
+
+### Access Protected Route
+
+Replace `<TOKEN>` with the access token returned by login.
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/data/protected \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>"
+```
+
+## Security Notes
+
+This is still a prototype. It now uses bcrypt password hashing and signed JWTs, but registered users are still stored in memory. Users disappear when the backend restarts.
+
+For production, the next important upgrades are:
+
+- Store users in a database.
+- Add proper user schema validation and duplicate-email checks at the database level.
+- Add refresh tokens or secure session management.
+- Prefer HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookies over `localStorage` for sensitive tokens.
+- Add rate limiting for login and registration.
+- Add password reset and email verification.
+- Add automated tests.
